# Text is LF in every checkout. Git for Windows would otherwise check files out as
# CRLF (core.autocrlf=true), and a file that is hashed, signed or compared byte for
# byte -- a receipt, a digest-pinned fixture, a golden file -- would read differently
# on the owner's machine than in CI.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never converted, whatever the checkout: images and fonts, and the fixtures the tests
# pin by their bytes (five feed and catalog CSVs carry CRLF line endings on purpose).
*.png binary
*.ttf binary
tests/fixtures/** -text
